Xu Huang-Distinguished Instuctor
Earned a Master’s degree in Composition from the China Conservatory of Music on a full scholarship in 2012, with a minor in Piano.
Music H Studio founder; A member of China Electronic Music Composition Association; Former CCTV “Songba Music Library” Music Director; Repeatedly served as a judge of The Great China Youth Piano Competition, an oversea judge of “Chinese Voice”; And invited many pioneer music lectures.
Personal works(2009-2016)：
“Paradise walking” award and selected for the 15th International Electronic Music Festival, premiered in Beijing;
“Art of Microphone” award and selected for the 2nd Shanghai International Electronic Music Festival, premered in Shanghai;
“Yin” won the first prize of the “KYMA” Composer Music Competition in 2014 on behalf of the Central Conservatory of Music at the University of Oregon;
“Paradise” Central Academy of Music Youth Symphony Orchestra chief co-performance;
“Hearing Beijing” multimedia device project, exhibited in the China Millennium Monument;
“Meishan” a theme song created for the Hunan Provincial Government, included in the Chinese Record Company and published;
“Three Kinds of interactive music” papers published;
“Before Dawn”, “Daughter of Beautiful Times”, “Troubled Times” and so on, participated in many films and television dramas music production.
